      {
        "id": 201565,
        "name": "bolnerap",
        "username": "bolnerap",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bolnerap/{size}/6056_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-08-16T10:37:22.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Indianapolis local here. May I suggest a restaurant downtown to look into for this? Try Pearings - it's never particularly busy, it's open long hours, it's got bottled and tap beer despite being mostly a sandwich / frozen yogurt place, it's across the street from the mall, so you can get there mostly indoors from the convention center, and they have a REALLY LONG TABLE that I imagine would be good for gaming. I used to go there all the time because it's attached to the building I work in.</p><p>The address is 6 W. Washington Street. It's right next door to the Rock Bottom Restaurant &amp; Brewery.</p><p>Wish I'd checked this thread to offer the suggestion earlier, but maybe someone will see it.</p>",
